WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.320
ROHITH RAMKUMAR:
Welcome, everyone.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.060
For our session today,
I'm going to talk

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.400
about what we've been working
on in Google networking

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.850
to increase speed, reliability,
the locations you can connect

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:17.120
to us, and, of course, how
to manage those connections.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.550
We'll also cover our recently
announced partnership

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.860
with Cisco bringing
together SD-WAN

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.430
and the best of GCP cloud.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:28.100
Starting with our dedicated
Interconnect product

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.750
at Next 2019 last year, we
announced beta availability

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.540
for the 100 gigabit per
second dedicated Interconnect.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.660
Since then, it's become
generally available.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.060
100 gigabits per second
dedicated Interconnect

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.210
provides 10 times the capacity
of our previous Interconnect

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.690
offering and can be combined
into link aggregation groups

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.000
to bring massive
amounts of bandwidth.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.760
With 100 gigabit per second
dedicated Interconnect,

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.530
you can scale your
connection capacity

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.600
to meet your particular
requirements,

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.810
connect up to 800 gig
transport circuits

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:02.210
for private cloud
traffic to Google Cloud

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:03.840
at any of our POPs.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.920
We're also working on increasing
packet per second performance

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.470
and making it easier to achieve
high SLA configurations.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.380
There will be more news
on this later this year.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.810
Although Google already
has enormous footprint,

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.410
we want to make it easier
and less expensive than ever

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:21.570
for customers to
connect to GCP globally.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.190
So we're aiming to
bring Interconnect

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:27.620
to over 30 more locations
worldwide by mid next year.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.890
When we're done with
the expansion program,

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.850
we will have brought
the number of locations

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:34.400
you can connect to
GCP to well over 100,

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.880
adding 50% more
locations in key places,

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.210
like Houston, Boston,
Berlin, Canberra,

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:45.630
and multiple locations in
Asia and the Middle East.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:48.750
Finding a suitable location
for you to connect to Google

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:52.440
is made easier through our
extensive partner ecosystem.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.080
You can now find the
optimum connectivity pathway

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.680
to Google Cloud platform from
any on-net building or data

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.260
center worldwide on the
new Cloud Pathfinder

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:04.990
app for Google Cloud
provided by [? Cloudseek. ?]

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.150
By enabling customers
like you with an app,

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:10.000
like Cloud Pathfinder
for Google Cloud,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.100
we've provided a
search-based interface

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.920
to make it easy to identify
which partners can provide

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.650
Interconnect connectivity
at points closest to you

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.810
on-prem to GCP.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:23.930
The app is available from all
mobile devices or your desktop.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:27.677
You can access the app for
free now via find.cloud/google.

00:02:31.413 --> 00:02:34.070
Moving onto our
Cloud VPN product,

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.530
if your needs are to
securely connect everywhere,

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.080
you can use GCP's Cloud VPN.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.660
Our newest offering,
High Availability VPN,

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:45.080
became generally available
in Q4 of last year.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:49.280
With HA VPN, you can connect
to your on-premises GCP

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.470
or other cloud environments
with an industry-leading SLA

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:56.480
of four nines catered for your
mission-critical workloads.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.360
With redundant tunnel
pairs, the extra nine

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:03.800
takes you from eight hours and
46 minutes of allowed downtime

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.320
per year to just 53 minutes.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:09.890
That's a 90% reduction
in allowed downtime.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:12.290
We're encouraging customers
to migrate their deployments

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:15.050
from classic to
HA VPN to achieve

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:18.720
a more reliable architecture.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.490
We've briefly covered
Google's network and the work

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:24.370
we've done to expand
the locations to connect

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.590
increasing the speed and
making your connections

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.380
secure and available.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:32.350
Now, we'd like to zoom out
a bit and talk about not

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.420
just connecting to
GCP, but the ability

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.590
to connect to places outside
of GCP using Google's backbone.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:41.685
And we're doing this initially
in partnership with Cisco.

00:03:41.685 --> 00:03:43.810
Here's a little video that
shares a little bit more

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:46.900
about the partnership we've
been working on with Cisco.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.050
- The network is the foundation
of hybrid and multi-cloud

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:51.430
business transformation.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:54.160
You need a turnkey solution to
securely bridge applications

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.140
to networks across
multiple clouds,

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:59.170
modernize your enterprise, and
reduce networking complexity

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.630
with the best of Cisco
and Google Cloud.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.250
Our joint solution
will automatically

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.260
provision a reliable
global network that

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.150
grows with your
needs, experience

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:09.670
simple and flexible
customer network access,

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:11.800
publish all of your
services in one place,

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.950
and seamlessly extend and tend
to enterprise applications,

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:17.649
deliver context aware and
identity-based security

00:04:17.649 --> 00:04:20.560
management, realize a
fully software-defined

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.000
end-to-end network.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.050
Get to know Cisco SD-WAN
Cloud Hub with Google Cloud.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.760
ROHITH RAMKUMAR:
So what we know is

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.610
that customers are increasingly
moving into the realities

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:32.620
of a multi-cloud world.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.420
Many surveys of
Enterprise customers

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.660
suggest that enterprises are
deploying their applications

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.090
increasingly across
multiple clouds.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.180
We believe that this is the
enterprise modernization

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:44.860
and digital
transformation journey.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:46.600
And it starts with
the network which

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.680
must enable agile access to
innovation promised by cloud,

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:54.250
as well as simplified models
for multi-cloud, multi-platform

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:55.540
deployments.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:58.930
The network must evolve to
provide agility, simplicity,

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:02.710
and openness that is needed
to power this transformation.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:05.920
To summarize, what we're seeing
is enterprises that are broadly

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:09.070
looking to create, connect,
and consume resources

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:11.980
across a number of
different environments,

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:15.070
creating them, leveraging the
best in-class technologies,

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:16.870
connecting them
from a single point,

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.270
and consuming them
on demand, including

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.280
the connectivity between them.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:24.190
When deployments span
multiple app environments,

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:27.610
enterprises need to maintain a
fairly precise set of controls.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:30.070
The joint solution
from Cisco and Google

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:33.460
addresses exactly these needs,
bringing the best of SD-WAN

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.830
together with the
intelligence of cloud in order

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.750
to enhance application
performance

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:41.590
and end user experience.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:44.170
What we're continuing
to see is a shift

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:47.620
from monolithic
architectures of legacy apps

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.200
on private on-prem
datacenter environments

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:54.160
to a microservices
architecture that are

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.750
deployed in and across clouds.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.470
We're also seeing an increase
in the use of top tier SaaS

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:01.930
applications becoming more
central to maintaining

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:03.910
enterprise productivity.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:07.210
The use of SD-WAN in
concert with cloud network

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:09.340
and intelligence across
these environments

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.860
means that corporate policies
and security postures

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:14.380
can be maintained even as
the application delivery

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.250
footprint changes.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.940
To further joint
interest, Google and Cisco

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:21.430
are expanding our partnership
through a unique solution

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:26.110
called Cisco SD-WAN Cloud
Hub with Google Cloud.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:28.420
We will enable
200,000 enterprises

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:31.030
to access the power of
Cisco's SD-WAN solution

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:35.080
extending it to GCP's cloud
while powering connectivity

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:38.080
over Google's network,
supporting new capabilities

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.530
such as allowing enterprises to
use Google's global network as

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:43.750
if it were their own.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:45.510
We've seen a number
of publications

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:48.180
already begin to detail
the power and potential

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.850
of the cloud hub solution,
as Cisco and Google integrate

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:55.380
SD-WAN and cloud to deliver
a unique value to customers.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.030
A few of those
publications and quotes

00:06:57.030 --> 00:07:00.190
have been shared on the slide.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.920
At a high level, with
the cloud hub solution,

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.710
enterprises can continue to
deploy their Cisco SD-WAN

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:11.140
footprint on-prem and via the
Cisco vManage solution extended

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:14.560
to, through, and within GCP
leveraging Google's network

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:17.170
to enhance connectivity
to things like their VPC

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.440
environment, third-party
SaaS services, and solutions

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.700
and other clouds.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:24.910
Here, we see three major pillars
of benefits for the cloud hub

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:29.560
solution related to flexibility
and simplicity, improved end

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:33.660
user experience, and risk
and compliance management.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.000
With the cloud hub
solution, connectivity

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.580
from on-prem to the
cloud hub is provisioned

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.800
in an automated fashion via
Cisco's vManaged controller

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:46.500
while capacity to the cloud hub
is provided on demand as well

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:50.520
as beyond the cloud
hub and how the cloud

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:55.320
hub accesses resources that
sit on cloud and beyond.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.990
Cisco Cloud Hub
essentially enables

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.600
elastic and dynamic
consumption of bandwidth

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.660
over Google's network.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.090
With service
directory, applications

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:08.480
can then be listed and have its
metadata shared with the SD-WAN

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.630
fabric so that the appropriate
delivery treatment can

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:17.130
be provided via the SD-WAN for
each application specifically.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:19.030
Also, from a
security perspective,

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:21.390
Cisco and Google
share the user context

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.670
to enhance the
ability for the SD-WAN

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:25.560
to maintain the appropriate
levels of access

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.160
to cloud apps and services.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:29.310
For example,
sharing such context

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:32.610
would allow access to be
blocked for a user connected

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.490
to a guest network within
a corporate environment

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:38.880
while accepting access
to apps running on cloud

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:41.370
for legitimate corporate users.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:44.860
Going into the solution
component specifically,

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:48.310
Cisco establishes a
presence in Google

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:51.160
at the relevant regions based
on the customer's deployment

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:52.000
needs.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.400
From there, the
cloud hub solution

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.950
can leverage Google's network
to connect to other cloud hubs

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:59.790
to enable transit and
hybrid connectivity.

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.890
But cloud hubs will also be able
to access the customer's VPC

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.500
environments and various
applications and services that

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.870
are relevant to the customer.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:09.940
Speaking of applications
and services,

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.850
enterprises can leverage service
directory through cloud hub

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:15.550
in order to access a
catalog and publish

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:18.220
a list of apps and
their properties,

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:21.700
like the need for low latency
transmission to the end user.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.650
From here, Cisco's
vManage retrieves

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:27.580
this information shared via
metadata on a per application

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.100
basis and then
enables the cloud hubs

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.620
to take the appropriate
traffic steering decisions

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:35.940
based on what's required
for a given application.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:41.000
Lastly with the Cisco Cloud
Hub and Google Cloud SD-WAN,

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.360
they shared contextual access to
corporate user and app identity

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:47.090
to be able to provide
enhanced access to the most

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:49.760
secure segments of
the enterprise network

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:52.640
to better manage risk
and maintain compliance.

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:55.200
To summarize,
Google and Cisco are

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.260
in a strategic
collaboration to build

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.180
what we believe will
be the industry's

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:03.560
first application-centric
multi-cloud fabric.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:06.500
We believe this will help change
the model by which enterprises

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.270
choose to connect to
the resources that

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:09.990
matter to them the most.

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:13.280
In this solution, Google
provides reliable connectivity

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:15.940
over its network bridging
the enterprise network

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:21.430
to cloud applications and
services on GCP and beyond.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.060
Thank you.

